00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:25.660
table yet and that we actually need to
have pathways through which people can

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:30.400
come and join. So these are not intended
to be static entities. So for example let

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:34.120
me give an example. At AAAS we have a
social media working group meets Monday

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:37.990
morning 11:00 a.m. and that transects
across all the dreaded silos, so it's

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:42.670
various editors, various program
directors, and so on, all of whom don't

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:47.050
have enough time on their own to keep up
with all the changes in social media. So

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:52.390
they join this working group once a week, one, to share current campaigns things

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:56.080
that are going on so that everybody else
in the organization who's online knows

00:12:56.080 --> 00:13:00.040
about it but, two, to talk about the
